# Content conventions

- `content/source/cv.yaml` is read-only fact. Never edit, normalize, correct,
  reorder, enrich, or write to it.
- Factual production text must be loaded through a typed source path and equal
  the source value exactly. Selection and sequencing are allowed; shortening,
  paraphrase, combination, and inferred case-study prose are not.
- `/resume/` covers every publishable source leaf. Unknown/missing fields,
  dropped values, or changed rendered digests fail the build.
- Neutral UI labels live in a reviewed allowlist and must not imply seniority,
  scale, impact, ownership, verification, or technology absent from the source.
- Do not use an LLM to author production factual copy.
- Do not extract CV numbers into decorative metrics. Keep them inside the exact
  source statement.
- Existing canonical contact/location values may render only on
  portfolio/résumé routes. Public deployment requires owner confirmation; local
  builds do not. Never copy those values into fixtures, snapshots, logs,
  telemetry, analytics, or demo content.
- All scenario, policy example, identity, tool, trace, approval, and test values
  are visibly synthetic. Use reserved example/invalid domains where needed.
- Maintain public-source entries for clean-room governance concepts. Do not use
  employer artifacts, inferred workflows, names, or identifiers; omit anything
  with uncertain provenance.
- The lab is a new synthetic clean-room portfolio demonstration, not an
  employer deliverable and not proof of a résumé claim.
